# Per-bot TWAP history. The glob matters: each oracle's bot needs its OWN
# state file (two bots sharing one corrupts it), so the lean bot writes
# twap_state.lean.json and a bare `twap_state.json` rule would miss it.
twap_state*.json
*.egg-info/
.venv/
contracts/.venv/
contracts/build/
.vercel

# secrets / throwaway keys (never commit — see SECURITY.md)
.env.*
*.mnemonic
tests/.env.testnet

# private working notes (research, prior art) — never commit
*.private.md

# Algorand contract build output (regenerated by `algokit compile`)
magnetfi/v2/contracts/smart_contracts/artifacts/

# TypeScript incremental build cache — regenerated by every build, so it
# churns on every commit and conflicts on every pull. Local-only.
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
